employer_name_irc = The Iron Ring Company
employer_name_irc_command = Iron Ring
employer_description_irc = Founded as a Shinohara subsidiary, the Iron Ring Company later became an independent salvage supplier. It operates yards and recovery crews around recurrence-active wreck fields, selling equipment to anyone able to pay and deliver salvage on schedule.

employer_name_pta = Pang Tai Arms
employer_name_pta_command = Pang Tai Navalcomm
employer_description_pta = An independent arms maker from beyond Crescent that competes through reliable, affordable infantry weapons and small-vessel systems. Its Taypani contracts use neutral brokers and Free Company routes to avoid dependence on one corporate supply chain.

employer_name_icm = Ihijerika Civilian Manufacturing
employer_name_icm_command = Ihijerika Centcomm
employer_description_icm = A Taypani producer of civilian vessels, luxury goods, and basic survival equipment. Its inexpensive, repairable hulls are common among spacers starting out or rebuilding after a costly Turning.

employer_name_ipc = Interdyne Pharmaceuticals
employer_name_ipc_command = Interdyne Command
employer_description_ipc = A core TFCF member providing trauma medicine, pharmaceuticals, cybernetics, cloning support, insurance, body recovery, and TraumaSec protection. A paid client is treated as a responsibility, though the policy terms can be predatory.

employer_name_gsc = Gorlex Security Consulting
employer_name_gsc_command = Gorlex Command
employer_description_gsc = The TFCF's principal armed contractor. Gorlex provides escorts, bounty work, interdiction, boarding, deniable raids, and contract enforcement; whether an operation is called privateering or piracy usually depends on whose paperwork is recognized.

employer_name_saw = Shipbreaker Astronautics Workers Union
employer_name_saw_command = SAW Crew Council
employer_description_saw = A worker-owned TFCF collective providing mining, salvage, shipbreaking, repair, material recovery, and improvised construction. Its crews reject both corporate bosses and automatic subordination to distant revolutionary committees.

employer_name_cdt = Cyberdawn Technologies
employer_name_cdt_command = Cyberdawn Command
employer_description_cdt = A TFCF technology and intelligence company specializing in signals, electronic warfare, intrusion, experimental weapons, recurrence calibration, precision systems, and psionic countermeasures. It promises results to the Federation without surrendering every proprietary method.

employer_name_scribes = The Imperial Charter of Scribes
employer_name_scribes_command = Saintsworn Scholastic Office
employer_description_scribes = A chartered Imperial body of researchers, archivists, navigators, and technical specialists. It preserves certified baselines and records, then adapts advanced systems to the phase conditions of the current Taypani cycle.

# Legacy employer IDs retained for character compatibility; canonical noble houses remain player-created space.
employer_name_osteen = Chartered Burgher Consortium
employer_name_osteen_command = Olywier Charter Commerce Office
employer_description_osteen = A consortium of lenders, guild masters, warehouse operators, and freight brokers recognized under Count Olywier's charter. It finances extraction and military supply while defending burgher contracts against arbitrary requisition.

employer_name_vogsburg = Olywier Charter Household
employer_name_vogsburg_command = Edelheim Court
employer_description_vogsburg = The administrative and household service surrounding Count Olywier Rabenau's Crescent charter. It supports the court, archives, subordinate privileges, military obligations, and political bargains that turn the Count's seal into practical government.

employer_name_imperialnavy = Imperial Charter Garrison
employer_name_imperialnavy_command = Lord Admiral's Command
employer_description_imperialnavy = The military arm of Count Olywier's regional charter, combining household personnel, noble retainers, chartered auxiliaries, hired specialists, Saintsworn personnel, and locally raised troops under the Lord Admiral's operational command.

employer_name_homeguard = Union Homeguard
employer_name_homeguard_command = League Naval Command
employer_description_homeguard = The professional Crescent military descended from local cadres trained by Workers' Union officers during the first uprising. The Homeguard is a Crescent force using Union doctrine, not an imported army.

employer_name_vrachev = Alyans Vrachev
employer_name_vrachev_command = League Medical Command
employer_description_vrachev = A revolutionary medical and research organization that treats workers, supports Homeguard operations, and performs the current-cycle calibration needed to keep advanced Taypani medicine functioning.

employer_name_sindikat = Sindikat Inzenjera
employer_name_sindikat_command = League Industrial Command
employer_description_sindikat = An engineering labor organization responsible for construction, repair, munitions, vessels, and maintenance of critical League infrastructure under worker, Union, or wartime administration.

employer_name_logistics = Taypani Logistics Union
employer_name_logistics_command = League Logistics Command
employer_description_logistics = The NCWL's freight and allocation network, moving fuel, ammunition, salvage, industrial material, and civilian necessities between the active front, neutral markets, and the secure rear in Chengridz.
